+Two speeds (RULES). A harder set the same night, 30 videos and 35 staged changes
+from news to music and back: "careful", the first rule, took 29 s to enter and
+24 s to leave, with 2.5 false entries over 17 videos that are not music. "fast"
+took 15 s and 11 s, with 5 false entries on the SAME 3 videos (Inception, Interstellar,
+a Pixar montage) and no more time wrongly on music, for about twice the CPU. Needing
+2 of 3 at the slower rate looked as quick but also fell for Top Gear, a BBC
+documentary, commercials and football, and is why this one scores more often
+rather than asking for less evidence.
